hildren associated with the Zodiac case. He was fired from elementary schools for molesting children in March/April 1968, eight months before the first Vallejo murder [Data: Entities (398, 478, 486, 624); Relationships (1164, 1170, 1575)]. He was later arrested for molestation in January 1975 [Data: Entities (398, 626); Relationships (1576)]. His past work at elementary schools also suggested he would have knowledge of bus routes, which were relevant to some Zodiac threats [Data: Entities (484); Relationships (1165)].\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Handwriting and Physical Trait Comparisons\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Investigators conducted extensive comparisons of Allen's characteristics to those of the Zodiac killer. His handwriting and personal traits were compared to the Zodiac letters, with a theory suggesting he might have written them with his non-dominant hand [Data: Entities (414); Relationships (1009)]. Physical attributes such as shoe and glove size were also subjects of comparison [Data: Entities (411)]. However, Allen did not strongly resemble the composite sketch of the Zodiac killer based on witness descriptions from San Francisco, according to some witnesses [Data: Entities (480); Relationships (1169)].\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Unresolved Aspects and Allen's Death\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Despite being the primary suspect, Arthur Leigh Allen died of a heart attack in 1992 before he could be arrested for the murders [Data: Entities (398)]. DNA tests conducted on Zodiac envelopes did not match his DNA [Data: Entities (398)]. Furthermore, items belonging to victim Stine, such as his wallet and keys, were not found in Allen's trailer during searches [Data: Entities (631, 632); Relationships (1580, 1581)]. His trailer was cleaned out and moved to Santa Rosa on August 7, 1971 [Data: Entities (628); Relationships (1578)].\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Technical Knowledge Relevant to Zodiac Threats\",\n      \"explanation